    "은퇴" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Retirement"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "은퇴 때 %@원 → %@원" : {
      "comment" : "A comparison of retirement savings (peak and end) between a baseline and a recommended plan. The first argument is the age at which the recommended plan ends. The second argument is the age at which the baseline ends.",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated" : true,
      "localizations" : {
        "ko" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "은퇴 때 %1$@원 → %2$@원"
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "At retirement %@ won → %@ won"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "은퇴 후 매달 이 금액을 쓴다면, 구체적으로 뭘 누리고 싶은가요? 그게 진짜 당신인지, 아니면 남의 사진 속 장면인지 한번 가려보세요." : {
      "comment" : "A message for the \"Bucket List\" tip.",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated" : true,
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "If you spend this amount each month after retirement, what exactly do you want to enjoy? Check whether that's really you, or a scene from someone else's photo."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "은퇴 후 받고 싶은 ‘목표’ 패시브 인컴(배당·월세·이자 등)이에요. 여정 탭 ‘패시브 인컴 목표 달성률’의 기준이 됩니다. 비워두면 ‘은퇴 후 월 생활비’로 자동으로 맞춰요. 지금 실제로 받는 패시브 인컴은 자산 탭에 등록한 배당주·월세 부동산 등에서 자동 합산됩니다." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "The ‘target’ passive income (dividends, rent, interest, etc.) you want after retirement. It's the basis for ‘Passive income goal progress’ on the Journey tab. If blank, it's matched to ‘Monthly living costs after retirement’. Passive income you actually receive now is added up from dividend stocks, rental property and so on registered on the Assets tab."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "은퇴 후 월 생활비" : {
      "comment" : "A label describing the monthly living expenses after retirement.",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated" : true,
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Monthly living costs after retirement"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "은퇴 후 월 생활비 %@원을 모두 커버 · 월 %@원 여유 🎉" : {
      "comment" : "A celebratory message when the user's monthly passive income is enough to cover their target monthly living expenses.",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated" : true,
      "localizations" : {
        "ko" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "은퇴 후 월 생활비 %1$@원을 모두 커버 · 월 %2$@원 여유 🎉"
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Covers all %@ won of monthly living costs after retirement · %@ won to spare 🎉"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "은퇴 후 월 생활비 %@원의 %@ 커버 · 월 %@원 부족" : {
      "comment" : "A bar graph showing how much of the user's retirement savings will cover their monthly living expenses. The first argument is the percentage of the retirement savings that will cover the monthly living expenses. The second argument is the target monthly living expenses. The third argument is the shortfall, or the amount by which the user's savings are insufficient to cover their monthly living expenses.",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated" : true,
      "localizations" : {
        "ko" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "은퇴 후 월 생활비 %1$@원의 %2$@ 커버 · 월 %3$@원 부족"
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Covers %2$@ of your %1$@ won monthly costs after retirement · %3$@ won short a month"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "은퇴 후 월 생활비는 일을 그만둔 뒤 매달 쓰고 싶은 돈이에요.\n안전 인출률은 모은 돈에서 해마다 꺼내 써도 원금이 오래 버티는 비율이에요. 흔히 4%를 써요(‘4% 룰’ — 30년 동안 버틴다는 미국 연구에서 나온 값). 낮출수록 안전하지만 목표 금액이 커져요.\n목표 금액 = 한 해 생활비(월×12) ÷ 안전 인출률. 나이를 넣으면 여정 탭에 기간별 목표가 표시돼요." : {
      "comment" : "A longer description of the goal settings.",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated" : true,
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Monthly living costs after retirement is what you want to spend each month once you stop working.\nSafe withdrawal rate is the share of your savings you can take each year while the principal lasts a long time. 4% is common (the ‘4% rule’, from US research on lasting 30 years). Lower is safer but makes the target bigger.\nTarget = a year's living costs (monthly × 12) ÷ safe withdrawal rate. Enter your age and the Journey tab shows goals by period."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "은퇴까지" : {
      "comment" : "A label that displays the number of years until retirement.",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated" : true,
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Until retirement"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "음영은 수익률이 해마다 출렁일 때의 ‘가운데 50%%’ 범위예요(연 변동성 %@%% 가정). 미래는 선 하나가 아니라 이 폭 안에서 움직여요 — 시간이 갈수록 넓어지죠." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "The shading is the ‘middle 50%%’ range when annual returns fluctuate (assuming %@%% annual volatility). The future isn't a single line; it moves within this band — and it widens over time."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "음영은 열에 여덟이 들어오는 범위예요. 기간이 길수록 넓어져요." : {
      "comment" : "Text displayed below the chart.",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated" : true,
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "The shading is the range that covers eight in ten outcomes. It widens the longer the period."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "이 가격이 되면 판다 (1%@당, 원)" : {
      "comment" : "A text field for setting the price at which to sell an asset. The argument is the string “개” or the string “주”.",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated" : true,
